So now, since we have a lot of string functions, I'm going to go and divide them into categories based

00:04.800 --> 00:05.520
on the purpose.

00:05.560 --> 00:10.160
So for example we have a group of functions that's going to go and manipulate the string values.

00:10.160 --> 00:13.160
So we have concatenation upper lower replace and so on.

00:13.160 --> 00:15.320
And another group where we have only one function.

00:15.320 --> 00:18.240
It is where we can do calculations on the string values.

00:18.240 --> 00:22.720
And the last group, it is all about how to extract something from a string value.

00:22.760 --> 00:25.400
And here we have three functions left right substring.

00:25.400 --> 00:28.520
So now let's go and start with the first group about the data manipulation.

00:28.520 --> 00:30.800
And the first function we have here concat.

00:34.720 --> 00:35.120
All right.

00:35.120 --> 00:37.720
So what is exactly concat or concatenation.

00:37.720 --> 00:41.880
It's going to go and combine multiple string values into one value.

00:41.880 --> 00:45.080
So if you have multiple things you can put everything in one value.

00:45.080 --> 00:46.680
So let's have a very simple example okay.

00:46.720 --> 00:49.240
So now let's say that you have one value called Michael.

00:49.240 --> 00:50.560
So here you have the first name.

00:50.600 --> 00:53.800
And you have totally separated value for the last name.

00:53.800 --> 00:55.960
Another column where you have a value like Scott.

00:56.000 --> 00:57.160
And now you say you know what?

00:57.160 --> 01:00.360
It makes no sense to have the first name separated from the last name.

01:00.360 --> 01:05.690
I would like to go and combine them in one value so you can go and use the concat in order to combine

01:05.690 --> 01:10.210
those two values or multiple values into one single value, like Michael Scott.

01:11.410 --> 01:13.410
I think that pretty much sums it up.

01:14.370 --> 01:19.250
So it is nicer to see their full name in one value instead of having like two columns for that.

01:19.290 --> 01:20.090
So that's it.

01:20.090 --> 01:22.050
This is why we need the Concatenations.

01:22.090 --> 01:24.650
Now let's go back to SQL in order to try that out.

01:24.690 --> 01:24.890
Okay.

01:24.930 --> 01:26.330
So now we have the following task.

01:26.370 --> 01:31.050
Show a list of customers first names together with their country in one column.

01:31.050 --> 01:33.250
So that means we have to make a list of customers.

01:33.250 --> 01:35.370
And we have to combine two columns in one.

01:35.370 --> 01:37.490
So let's start writing the query select.

01:37.490 --> 01:42.410
We need the first name the country from the table customers.

01:42.410 --> 01:44.050
So first let's go and execute this.

01:44.050 --> 01:46.050
Now as you can see we have a list of customers.

01:46.050 --> 01:51.050
But the issue here the first name and the countries those two informations are in different columns.

01:51.050 --> 01:53.610
But the task says they should be in one column.

01:53.610 --> 01:57.610
So now in order to combine those two things we have to use the concatenate function.

01:57.610 --> 01:58.810
So concat.

01:58.850 --> 02:00.370
So we're going to start with the first argument.

02:00.370 --> 02:05.190
It's going to be the first name and then the country like this, and we're going to give it a name,

02:05.190 --> 02:07.310
let's call it like this name country.

02:07.870 --> 02:09.670
Now let's go and execute it.

02:09.670 --> 02:11.710
Now in the output you can see we have a new column.

02:11.710 --> 02:13.070
It's called Name Country.

02:13.070 --> 02:15.630
And we have both of the informations in one column.

02:15.630 --> 02:18.030
So we have Maria Germany join USA.

02:18.190 --> 02:21.950
But it doesn't really look good because there is like no spacing between them.

02:21.950 --> 02:27.750
Now we can go and make some separation between them by just adding one more thing in between.

02:27.750 --> 02:29.710
Like for example maybe space.

02:29.710 --> 02:35.670
So now we are concatenating the first name together with a space this over here and then the country.

02:35.670 --> 02:37.110
So let's go and execute it.

02:37.110 --> 02:41.030
Now as you can see, we have nice separations between the first name and the country.

02:41.030 --> 02:46.030
And of course you can go and add different separations like maybe minus or underscore and you will get

02:46.030 --> 02:46.830
the same effect.

02:46.830 --> 02:52.150
So with that we have a list of customers where we have the first name together with the country in one

02:52.150 --> 02:52.470
column.

02:52.470 --> 02:53.790
As you can see, it is very simple.

02:53.790 --> 02:56.390
This is how you combine two columns in one.

02:56.390 --> 02:58.270
It is really nice and easy transformation.

